y":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"the word \"COLUMN_VALUE\" is an implicit column name from the column-valued table, not a keyword on its own.\r\n\r\nensure the fix for #8827 is in place so that bind names are correct.\r\n\r\n```py\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import select, func, create_engine\r\n\r\nfoobar_col = func.SYS.ODCIVARCHAR2LIST(\"foo\", \"bar\", \"baz\").column_valued(\r\n    \"foobar\"\r\n)\r\nsnap_col = func.SYS.ODCIVARCHAR2LIST(\"snap\", \"crackle\", \"pop\").column_valued(\r\n    \"snap\"\r\n)\r\n\r\nmy_query = select(foobar_col, snap_col)\r\n\r\ne = create_engine(\"oracle+cx_oracle://scott:tiger@oracle18c/xe\", echo=\"debug\")\r\n\r\nwith e.begin() as conn:\r\n    res = conn.execute(my_query)\r\n    print(res.fetchall())\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\nsqlalchemy.exc.DatabaseError: (cx_Oracle.DatabaseError) ORA-00918: column ambiguously defined\r\n[SQL: SELECT COLUMN_VALUE foobar, COLUMN_VALUE snap \r\nFROM TABLE (SYS.ODCIVARCHAR2LIST(:ODCIVARCHAR2LIST_1, :ODCIVARCHAR2LIST_2, :ODCIVARCHAR2LIST_3)) foobar, TABLE (SYS.ODCIVARCHAR2LIST(:ODCIVARCHAR2LIST_4, :ODCIVARCHAR2LIST_5, :ODCIVARCHAR2LIST_6)) snap]\r\n[parameters: {'ODCIVARCHAR2LIST_1': 'foo', 'ODCIVARCHAR2LIST_2': 'bar', 'ODCIVARCHAR2LIST_3': 'baz', 'ODCIVARCHAR2LIST_4': 'snap', 'ODCIVARCHAR2LIST_5': 'crackle', 'ODCIVARCHAR2LIST_6': 'pop'}]\r\n```\r\n\r\nthe implementation mis-uses the word \"COLUMN_VALUE\" as a keyword, which it's not.   That's \"col label\" syntax above, effectively.  \r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url"